Bard wrote:
> Found some boots of speed early in my current game. Since this is
> something I'll likely wear the whole game, I want to enchant/foo-proof
> them, but which to do first? Is the benefit of fooproofing worth the
> extra AC point trade off in early game? how about for artifact weapons
> (mjolnir). 
> 
> 10lvl human valk AC:-9 fwiw.
> 
> Thoughts?
> 

Speed boots don't need fireproofing (though I do it; just for cosmetical
reasons) since the one point lost will be compensated by the enchantment.
Different thing with, e.g., a cloak of protection (or a robe) that may
lose up to 3 (resp. 2) points of AC and is well worth fireproofing.

Artifact weapons from your god are always fooproof, and you, as a Valkyrie,
got Mjollnir from your god, I suspect; so no action necessary to fooproof
it. OTOH, if you find an artifact weapon randomly on the floor (and it is
not yet fooproof) then you have (at least) two choices; either fooproof
it, because there are several level of weapon damage that reduce the
effectiveness increasingly, or have a second weapon at hand that does not
rust (a silver saber) to hit the acidic monsters. (The saber is also very
useful to use against demons. But it requires that you have the proficiency
to use that type of weapon, of course; Valkyrie gets "basic" in sabers.)

